$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 desc_overview {
  m_sTitle "Overview"
  m_sTextData "A reduced Soviet motorized rifle platoon carries out a prepared defense against an attacking US airborne force."\
  ""\
  ""\
  "Slotting considerations:"\
  "- On the Soviet side, all 3 squads should be slotted to some extent. Not slotting some of them will leave gaps in the defense."\
  "- BTRs may be single-manned by the gunner (recommended if at minimum), having a driver allows for additional situational awareness (commander periscope) and optional maneuverability."\
  "- Playing as CO on either side in this mission is not particularly difficult. The Soviet commander has to manage execution of an already mostly pre-planned defense, and for the US CO it is technically enough to simply designate some approaches and general concept."\
  ""\
  "US players should expect to die, but they have respawns."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
 }
 brief_ussr {
  coords 0 0 0
  m_sTitle "Briefing"
  m_sTextData "<h2>Situation</h2>"\
  "<b>a. Enemy Forces</b>"\
  "US airborne infantry, total strength estimated at 1-2 platoons."\
  "Situated somewhere to the south, an imminent attack is likely."\
  "<b>a. Friendly Forces</b>"\
  "One reduced platoon of motorized rifle troops with 2 BTRs."\
  "The platoon previously established a defensive strongpoint on elevated terrain near a farmstead, with prepared defensive positions facing south (vehicle dugouts, fighting positions for shooting from prone position, razor wire, 2 small minefields)."\
  ""\
  "<h2>Mission</h2>"\
  "Your platoon is ordered to defend against the attack, using the platoons defensive positions."\
  "The defense is considered a failure if the enemy manages to occupy the platoon command post established at the farm."\
  "It is likely that if the enemy would pause the attack if still unable to take the strongpoint after 30 minutes."\
  ""\
  "<h2>Execution</h2>"\
  "There is an established defensive plan (see map) describing general squad and vehicle positions. It should be taken as a basis without large initial deviations, but further adjustments can be made as required during the defense."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "USSR"
  }
 }
 desc_notes {
  coords 0 0 0
  m_sTitle "Notes"
  m_sTextData "- 2 minute setup timer restricting US"\
  "- US have 15 respawns"\
  ""\
  "Some rules:"\
  "- Soviet players may NOT cut down trees and bushes in large quantities. A couple per squad is fine (if you need to get a bush out of the way), but don't cut down larger swaths of trees."\
  "- Soviet players should use the established defensive positions, don't fall back onto the objective unless it becomes necessary. Also, don't barricade the objective."\
  ""\
  "Note on Soviet trenches: To use them properly, make sure you are in a prone position and not too far forward. Leave some room to your front, otherwise you will not be able to use your weapon properly."\
  ""\
  "Note for GMs: I am not sure how well balanced the amount of AI spawning is. I think it will be fine, but if it turns out to be insufficient, you may spawn an additional fire team occasionally, just don't overdo it."\
  ""\
  "End conditions:"\
  "- US Victory: Circled area under control for 1 minute"\
  "- USSR Victory: 30 minutes pass"
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 1
 }
 brief_us {
  coords 0 0 0
  m_sTitle "Briefing"
  m_sTextData "<h2>Situation</h2>"\
  "<b>a. Enemy Forces</b>"\
  "Reduced platoon of motorized rifle troops with 2 BTRs."\
  "It previously established a defensive strongpoint near the farmstead (elevated terrain), with prepared defensive positions facing south (including vehicle dugouts, fighting positions; within 200m of the FLET razor wire and possibly some mines). Their command post appears to be the farmstead building."\
  ""\
  "<b>a. Friendly Forces</b>"\
  "US airborne infantry, total strength of 2 understrength platoons."\
  "Only one platoon is available at the moment, another will join the assault some time later."\
  ""\
  "<h2>Mission</h2>"\
  "Your platoon is ordered to seize the Soviet strongpoint."\
  "The assault is considered a success if the platoon command post established at the farmstead is taken."\
  "If unable to seize the defensive position within 30 minutes, you are ordered to retreat and await the arrival of follow on forces."\
  ""\
  "<h2>Service Support</h2>"\
  "There is a crate with some explosives, intended for removal of barbed wire and mines. Don't take all at once!"\
  ""\
  ""\
  "<h2>Gameplay Notes</h2>"\
  "You basically represent an element of the platoon and are assaulting the defensive position along with periodically spawning AI squads."\
  "Expect to die and respawn possibly multiple times. Respawning players are NOT allowed to move on their own, you must wait for at least one other person."\
  "Due to the nature of the mission and reliance on respawns, it is recommended to not establish some rigid tactical plan and instead designate routes which respawning teams should pick from. Probing multiple different approaches is recommended."\
  "If unconscious, feel free to use the respawn button as there is no medic."\
  "Try to balance out your respawns. If you're running out and there's still lots of time left, play it slow."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "US"
  }
 }
}